🔐 AFTER SSH LOGIN – HOW TO FIND A FILE IN LINUX
✅ CASE 1: find COMMAND IS WORKING (BEST & FASTEST)
🔹 Why use find?

Searches the entire filesystem

Works even if you don’t know the file location

CEH exam-friendly

🔹 Command (Recommended)
find / -name Netnormal.txt 2>/dev/null

🔹 Explanation
Part	Meaning
/	Start search from root
-name	Search by exact filename
2>/dev/null	Hide permission errors
🔹 If filename case is unknown
find / -iname netnormal.txt 2>/dev/null

🔹 If only extension is known
find / -name "*.txt" 2>/dev/null

🔹 After locating file
cat /path/to/Netnormal.txt

❌ CASE 2: find COMMAND NOT WORKING / RESTRICTED

This happens when:

Limited user permissions

BusyBox / restricted shell

find binary missing

👉 DO NOT PANIC — CEH expects you to know alternatives.

🔁 METHOD 1: locate (If Available)
🔹 Why?

Uses an indexed database → very fast

locate Netnormal.txt


⚠️ If database is outdated:

sudo updatedb

🔁 METHOD 2: Manual Directory Enumeration (EXAM-FRIENDLY)
🔹 Why?

CEH labs usually store files in predictable locations

Check these first 👇

ls
pwd


Then:

ls /home
ls /home/*
ls /tmp
ls /var/www
ls /opt

🔹 Typical CEH file locations
Location	Reason
/home/user/	User-owned sensitive files
/tmp/	Temporary attacker files
/var/www/html/	Web-related flags
/opt/	Custom apps
/root/	If root access
🔁 METHOD 3: grep (VERY IMPORTANT FALLBACK)
🔹 Why?

If you know partial content, you can search inside files.

grep -R "Netnormal" / 2>/dev/null


Or search all .txt files:

grep -R "normal" /home 2>/dev/null

🔁 METHOD 4: Using ls -R (Recursive Listing)
ls -R /home 2>/dev/null | grep Netnormal

🔁 METHOD 5: Check Recently Modified Files (SMART TRICK)
find / -type f -mtime -2 2>/dev/null


Why?

CEH files are often recently created

🔁 METHOD 6: Check Environment Hints
history
env


Why?

Sometimes path is leaked in command history

🔥 BEST EXAM STRATEGY (ORDER TO TRY)

1️⃣ find / -name filename 2>/dev/null
2️⃣ find / -iname "*.txt"
3️⃣ Check /home, /tmp, /var/www
4️⃣ grep -R
5️⃣ ls -R | grep

⚠️ COMMON CEH EXAM MISTAKES

❌ Forgetting 2>/dev/null
❌ Searching /root without root
❌ Wasting time brute-searching whole system blindly

🧠 QUICK CHEAT SHEET
# Best
find / -iname Netnormal.txt 2>/dev/null

# If find fails
